WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.910
(light music)

00:00:07.051 --> 00:00:10.101
- Where in modern life can we be accepted

00:00:10.101 --> 00:00:12.768
by others, in all of our facets?

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:16.000
The beautiful and the ugly.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.069
The comfortable and the uncomfortable.

00:00:19.069 --> 00:00:21.501
How do we open that Pandora's box?

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.001
And dance with it?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.110
My name is Vangeline,
and I am a Butoh artist.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:43.440
Butoh is an art form that was
born in Japan in the 1950s,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.051
now it is a global art form.

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:49.069
For me, Butoh is the dance of darkness.

00:00:49.069 --> 00:00:51.669
The dance of the subconscious.

00:00:51.669 --> 00:00:54.389
I think that body and mind and spirit

00:00:54.389 --> 00:00:56.331
are completely connected.

00:00:56.331 --> 00:00:59.021
When we access the body through repetition

00:00:59.021 --> 00:01:01.149
there is a part of the
mind that surrenders

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:03.816
and we begin to access emotions.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.930
There is no Homo erectus anymore.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.450
Butoh training is really,
really, really challenging.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.010
To be pushed to the limit, to that extent,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.541
and encouraged to have an
encounter with the self

00:01:19.541 --> 00:01:21.821
is not an easy endeavor.

00:01:21.821 --> 00:01:23.851
But it's a particularly acute challenge

00:01:23.851 --> 00:01:26.518
for people who are incarcerated.

00:01:33.061 --> 00:01:35.880
I started my work in
correctional facilities

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.463
with Butoh in 2006.

00:01:38.691 --> 00:01:39.941
Ah, yeah, nice.

00:01:41.341 --> 00:01:43.971
The classes at Edgecombe
are very powerful,

00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:46.341
they're also a process.

00:01:46.341 --> 00:01:48.120
And in the correctional facilities

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.181
it's a very volatile environment.

00:01:51.181 --> 00:01:54.431
My agenda is to start from blank slate.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.661
It's not my place to judge them.

00:01:57.661 --> 00:01:59.965
It's my place to provide a space

00:01:59.965 --> 00:02:02.865
of self-acceptance for them.

00:02:02.865 --> 00:02:05.585
A place for rehabilitation.

00:02:05.585 --> 00:02:08.377
Once they connect to the
sense of empowerment,

00:02:08.377 --> 00:02:10.535
that's a very important concept for people

00:02:10.535 --> 00:02:11.915
who are incarcerated.

00:02:11.915 --> 00:02:14.646
Self-knowledge, self-power.

00:02:14.646 --> 00:02:16.985
How can I be in control of my body

00:02:16.985 --> 00:02:21.662
that is essentially being
controlled by the states?

00:02:21.662 --> 00:02:24.103
The ones that keep coming back and repeat,

00:02:24.103 --> 00:02:25.785
and believe in the repetition and

00:02:25.785 --> 00:02:28.523
start on a path of commitment,

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:30.356
achieve great results.

00:02:32.303 --> 00:02:33.833
It's a dance full of guts.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:35.923
It's a dance full of soul.

00:02:35.923 --> 00:02:36.840
It's magic.

